export anchor SketchWireframeStyle:
    number: 34
    screen: TaskBoard
    name: Sketch wireframe
    idea: The app drawn as a pencil wireframe on dotted paper, wobbly hand-drawn boxes in greyscale with one blue pen for the things that need attention.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #fdfdfb, the page with a 24px dot grid in #d9d9d6
        sheet: #ffffff, boxes, cards and fields
        tray: #f3f3f1, the column fill
        pencil: #222222, text and every outline
        graphite: #595959, meta text and field labels
        smudge: #e4e4e4, hatching on Engineering labels and Done cards
        bluePen: #1a4fd6, the Add task button, the Overdue mark, the title underline and focus
        penWash: #e3ebff, hover, the focused row and the offset behind the primary button
    type:
        One handwriting stack for everything, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
        Marker Felt, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive. The project
        title is 34px bold, column titles 20px bold, card titles 17px bold,
        body 15px at 1.5 line height, meta 13px in graphite and field
        labels 13px. Code notes in the style sheet use a monospace stack.
    layout:
        The whole screen sits inside a sketched browser frame with three
        circles and a fake address bar. Inside, a crossed placeholder box
        and Brightwork sit on the left with Mara Okafor and a circled MO on
        the right. The title Mobile app 2.0 has a boxed At risk tag and a
        wavy blue pen underline. A row of labelled sketched dropdowns for
        Assignee, Label and Due, a Search tasks box and the Add task button
        on the right. Four dashed column trays hold wobbly white cards,
        each with the title, a label chip, the due date with a clock, a
        dashed divider and then a circled initial avatar with the name and
        points. Below 1040px the board has two columns, and below 640px one,
        with the controls stacking full width.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between cards, 24px between columns, 24px screen padding.
    density: Medium. The whole board fits one laptop screen.
    corners:
        No straight edges. Boxes use asymmetric elliptical radii such as
        255px 15px 225px 15px over 15px 225px 15px 255px, with two other
        variants alternated between cards. Avatars and count circles are
        slightly lopsided circles.
    borders:
        2px pencil outlines on cards, fields and buttons, plus a faint
        second stroke at 45 percent opacity slightly offset and roughened
        with an SVG turbulence filter. Columns use a 2px dashed outline.
        Card footers have a dashed divider.
    shadows: None, except the primary button which has a blue pen offset outline 3px right and 4px down.
    icons:
        Hand-drawn line icons with a 2px round stroke at text size,
        slightly uneven paths. Overdue is a triangle with an exclamation
        mark plus the word Overdue, circled by a blue pen loop. Done is a
        tick plus the word Done, with the title struck through and the card
        hatched. Unassigned is a dashed circle with a question mark. The
        logo is a crossed placeholder box.
    focus: A 2.5px dashed blue pen outline offset 4px. A focused field turns its outline blue and gets a pale blue offset block.
    tone: Plain sketch notes in sentence case, such as Add task, type to search, 5 pts.
